	-> Terraform : Terraform is an open-source Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tool developed by HashiCorp that allows users to define and manage cloud and on-premises infrastructure using human-readable configuration files.
		- terraform init
		- terraform providers...(Local, AWS etc.)
		- terraform plan (act as dry run)
		- terraform validate (ckecks that terraform file is right or not)
		- terraform apply (to apply terraform file)
		- terraform destroy (--target)
	
	-> EC2 using terraform :
		- terraform.tf
		- provider.tf
		- ec2.tf
		- variables.tf
		- outputs.tf
	
	-> meta arguments :
		- count > if u r using count = 2 then do aws_instance.my_instance[*].public_ip (in output.tf file)
		- for_each > for multiple instance with specified properties...
		  	> for_each = tomap ({
    			     	instance-1 = "t2.micro"
    				instance-2 = "t3.micro"
  		  		}) 
  		  	> then use key & value formate for the reference(in output.tf file) of this like below...
  		  		output ec2_public_ip {
  					value = [
    					for key in aws_instance.my_ec2 : key.public_ip 
  					]
				}
  		- depends_on > depends_on = [ aws_security_group.my-sec-group, aws_key_pair.my_key ]
  	
  	-> conditional statement : like if else
  		- variable.tf > 
  			variable "default_storage_size" {
  				default = 8
  				type    = number
			}
			variable env {
  				default = "prod"
  				type = string
			}
		- ec2.tf > 
			root_block_device {
    				volume_size = var.env == "prod" ? 10 : var.default_storage_size
    				volume_type = "gp3"
  			}
	
	-> terraform state : stored in > terrafrom.tfstate
		- terraform state list
		- remove state > terraform state rm <state_name>
		- import state > terraform import <state_name> <state_name_from_argument>
		- import state (instance) > terraform import <state_name> <instance_id>
			> also need to add this code in ec2.tf :
								resource "aws_instance" "new_my_ec2" {
    									instance_type = "unknown"
    									ami = "unknown"
								}
	
